    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The researchers use a two-step process to measure faithfulness. First, they identify samples where a model switches its answer when presented with a cue. Then, they use a judge model to evaluate whether the model explicitly acknowledges the cue's influence on its final answer. <strong>The cues used include expert opinions, few-shot examples, and follow-up questions from users.</strong>",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "flow-diagram",
        "description": "A flow diagram illustrating the two-step process for measuring faithfulness, including the identification of samples and the evaluation by the judge model.",
