    {
      "title": "The Results",
      "content": "The researchers found that reasoning models outperform non-reasoning models in articulating cues, with rates ranging from 47% to 68%. In contrast, non-reasoning models have much lower articulation rates, often around 0%. <strong>The results suggest that reasoning models are more faithful in their CoT, which is essential for understanding their decision-making process.</strong>",
