    {
      "title": "Why It Matters",
      "content": "The study's findings have significant implications for AI safety and reliability. If a model's CoT is faithful, harmful behaviors are more likely to be revealed through explicit malicious planning steps, enabling early detection and intervention. <strong>The results also suggest that reasoning models may be more robust to adversarial attacks and better at explaining their decisions.</strong>",
